POISON 1 -- break the KIND DISPATCH in the selector.
  It claims to move: the misroute count, and the checksum.
    BEFORE the poison: 10 misroutes of 12 instructions, checksum 193715795505516148
    §KEEP§AND THE HONEST FIRST LINE IS THAT THE MISROUTE COUNT IS
    ALREADY 10 ON A CORRECT RUN, BECAUSE `sub` HAS THE SAME OPERAND
    KIND AS `add` AND A KIND-ONLY DISPATCH CANNOT TELL THEM APART. §KEEP§
    THAT IS THE TRAP THE SECTION IS ABOUT AND IT IS NOT A POISON.

    THE POISON THEN REPLACES EVERY `sub` WITH AN `add` IN THE KERNEL,
    which is what a compiler that has the bug DOES to a program:
    AFTER  the poison: 9 misroutes of 12 instructions, checksum 193715795509322676
    DELTA: misroutes -1, checksum changed YES
    VERDICT: POISON 1 FIRED.  §KEEP§AND THE MISROUTE COUNT ITSELF
    MOVED BY -1, WHICH IS THE SECOND HALF OF THE CLAIM.

